YAAP - Mandevil the male human chaotic Barbarian (or My Second
Ascension)

After my very first ascension half a year ago (Arc-Hum-Mal-Neu)
followed by a voluntary break from playing, I decided to go for the
next letter in the alphabet, which is B for Barbarian. It was bit more
difficult than I expected, mainly because I kept suffering YASDs.
These often included very unfortunate events like falling into a pit
with wielded cockatrice at the top of the Wizard's Tower, eating
cockatrice egg or being overwhelmed by nasties summoned by Yeenoghu
summoned by sacrifice after I decided to get rid of him or getting
beaten to bloody pulp by trolls on a quest.

But then I finally broken series of YASDs and got a nice game going. I
bought a magic marker and bag of holding in Minetown and found another
one at Mine's End. Which, of course, meant that after thorougly
trashing my luck at Sokoban I got - you guessed it -- yet another bag
of holding. My pets kept dying on me, but later my pet dog ate
chameleon corpse and turned into a storm giant. Not that bad. Also on
dlvl 8 I found amulet of ESP, which is very useful throught the whole
game.

There was coaligned altar at dlvl 17, so I could fix my standing with
my god and get artifact. First sacrifice yielded Cleaver, the second
one reconciled me with Set.

Shortly after 20k turns at dlvl 19 I made the most significant
discovery of the whole game: I entered cross-aligned temple with
priestess, ghost and bones. Apparently, wizard SabreJon has attempted
to kill the priestess and failed, leaving behind treasure trove of
loot. Unfortunately, I had the stupid idea to use my new wealth in
money to buy protection from the priestess, who got angry and suddenly
I was in danger of being another addition to the local pile of bones.
Fortunately, I managed to escape the temple in one piece. I tried to
get my pet storm giant Benjamin to engage the priestess, but he was
too timid for that. It was clear, that direct confrontation with the
angry priestess in unfeasible, as she was hitting real hard and
blocking the escape route with swarms of insects -- good way to get
killed real fast. Then it ocurred to me, that on the way to the temple
I killed a cockatrice! So I raced there and back again in the hope
that I can use it to petrify my little angry hellcat. Before I even
got to strike her with c, she managed to beat hell out of me: from
full HP of 113 to red 32 at AC -10 in few blows. No wonder SabreJon
got killed. But the loot was absolutely worth the danger, there were
several extremely useful items: +2 SDSM and CoMR (both even
uncursed!), +4 Magicbane, water walking boots, ring of conflict, magic
lamp and some wands, potions and scrolls. There was also the Eye of
Aethiopica, but as chaotic I couldn't take it.

After sorting through the bones I went back to the Mine Town to unload
my money in its temple for 3 more points protection. Then I continued
to dive deeper. On dlvl 21 my pet storm giant stepped on a level
teleporter and was gone (much later found untame on some upper dlvl).
There was also a coaligned temple on dlvl 21. On Medusa (the "island"
version) I there was nurse on the island with staircase -- perfect
setting for a nurse dance, which increased my HP by whopping 47
points. Nice nurse!

Then I went to clear the castle, which was quite uneventful, except
one damned mind flayer, which sucked my brain a little, but leaving no
damage, apparently. I hoped to find silver sabre or silver spear in
the armory, but no luck. Since I still wasn't XL 14, I ventured into
VoTD in the hope of getting some wraith corpses there -- I got two,
along with two more mind flayers. So I was ready for the Quest. I
wished for ring of teleport control and levelported to the Quest
branch level. Of course, the first thing I found on the Quest was
another =oTC. And did I mention that I found three more magic markers
for total of four? RNG likes to tease me. Anyway, the Quest went
smoothly. Since I haven't found any silver weapon to two-weapon with,
I wished for a silver spear, which I enchanted to +5. I also got
crowned and received my Stormbringer.

I set off to Gehennom, which was rather boring. I tried the bottom-up
method with Asmodeus, but he kept digging down instead of teleporting
of upstairs. After running of charges he finally started to cooperate,
but unfortunately I managed to kill him. Orcus was greedy and wasted
all the charges of his wand of death before I got to kill him.
Generally, mapping the Gehennom was a nightmare. I remeber one level
where I just couldn't find upstairs. I had to levelport above to find
it. After I collected the Candelabrum from Vlad finished mapping, and
retrieved the Book of Dead I performed invocation, replaced my boots
of speeds with boots of jumping and levelported to the Sanctum. I
emerged in the graveyard area, so I could just as well come down via
stairs. Sanctum was easy, thanks in part to jumping. The priest was no
trouble and after I had AoY I quaffed cursed potion of gain level and
started running up. The way up was almost completely trouble free, I
had only two Rodney visitations and mysterious force did not ocur even
once.

Since I made the mistake of not learning a spell early enough to be
forgotten by the end game, I had to rely on my single saved potion of
confusion and tripe rations for confused scroll of detect gold. Other
than that the Elemental Planes were nominal, except incident on the
Plane of Air, where I got paralyzed in cloud and promptly swallowed by
air elemental, that pummeled me real bad. On Astral, I used conflict
and wand of teleport to clear my way. The second altar was the right
one. After ascending I realized, that I was not two-weaponing -- I was
only single-wielding my +6 Magicbane (skill=basic). That was why those
angels and priests were so hard to kill!

Overall, Barbarian is much, much easier in the early game with his
fast levelling up and great strength, but in the late game, I would
say that Arc is considerably more powerful. Barbarian is basic with
sabres, meaning Grayswandir with silver sabre does considerably less
damage. And the weapons Barbarian is expert with are either two-handed
or rather weak. Also there's no way Barbarian can cast identify spell.

